# Build context is the repo root (needed for the pnpm workspace + single root
# lockfile). Keep the context lean: ship only what `pnpm build` needs.

# Node
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/.verify
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS / CI / tooling
.git
.github
.claude
backlog

# Go backend + DB/migration tooling (not part of the frontend image)
cmd
internal
# ...except the stamped commit, which every SPA image serves at /build.txt so the
# deploy gate can tell the build under test from the one still being replaced. It
# lives under internal/ because go:embed cannot reach outside its own package
# directory, and one source of truth beats two files kept in sync by hand.
!internal/platform/buildsha.txt
migrations
db
# Python sidecar (sidecar/docling/Dockerfile is its own image, own build context)
sidecar
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
*.go
go.mod
go.sum
.env
.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
